#: freeports_dev.ci.suites.known_in:3 of
msgid ""
"The same rule the metric table follows: a repository is judged on what it"
" can actually answer for, so a formats repository is never asked about "
"the crate's doctests and never reports them as missing."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.suites.parse:3 of
msgid ""
"An outcome that is absent is a failure for the reason above: ``--suite "
"rust.unit`` with the colon left off says nothing about how the run went, "
"and the safe reading of nothing is not \"fine\"."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.suites.parse_outcome:3 of
msgid ""
"Deliberately asymmetric. This string is written by a shell variable in a "
"commit hook, and the one way this must not fail is by reading a word "
"nobody intended — an empty variable, a typo, a localised ``ok`` — as "
"success. Only the spellings listed here mean the suite passed."
msgstr ""

